# Winston 99 install

## Requirements
Linux, Apache (or nginx), PHP 8, MariaDB. Same class of host as WordPress.

## Steps
1. `git clone https://github.com/JesseSteele/Winston99.git` into the web folder.
2. Create a database and user.
3. Visit `install.php`.
   - DB host: `127.0.0.1` (not `localhost`)
   - Public host: everything after `https://` (example `write.pink/99`)
4. Log in as the Superintendent. Create a Facility, then an Administrator.

## Packages
Arch/Debian/RPM builders live in [99-package](https://github.com/PinkWrite/99-package). Same installer: `contrib/install`. `--webroot` sets destination; interactive does not ask for it. Verb uses `ink install winston99 -d domain.tld`.

## Mail
Edit `config.php` (`mail` key). SMTP password lives there on purpose. This is SysAdmin work.

## Update
```
php bin/update.php
```
or Superintendent / Admin locker **Update app**. Never overwrites `config.php`.

## Old dump
Do **not** run `install.php` on a live old database. The hand SQL lives on the [legacy branch](https://github.com/JesseSteele/Winston99/blob/legacy/README.md) as `sql/legacy-lift.sql`. Import the dump into an empty database, copy `config.sample.php` to `config.php` (`db.host` `127.0.0.1`), then `php bin/update.php`.

## Nginx
```
location = /config.php { deny all; }
location ~ ^/(lib|sql|bin|functions|dev)/ { deny all; }
```
